WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:12.067
The boys looked for a way to get to the Pharaoh’s pyramid.

2
00:00:12.068 --> 00:00:16.203
“There!” Akhom pointed.

3
00:00:16.204 --> 00:00:20.274
“We can sail to the Pharaoh’s pyramid in that boat!”

4
00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:23.576
“It looks like half a banana,”

5
00:00:23.577 --> 00:00:28.747
laughed Vinnie, describing the large sailing ship.

6
00:00:28.748 --> 00:00:33.086
“No. That small one,” corrected Akhom.

7
00:00:33.087 --> 00:00:37.376
The big boat was pulling a smaller one.

8
00:00:37.377 --> 00:00:41.085
Men were loading baskets onto the smaller boat.

9
00:00:41.086 --> 00:00:45.872
“Someone special must be going to visit the site,” said Akhom.

10
00:00:45.873 --> 00:00:49.211
“How do you know?” asked Vinnie.

11
00:00:49.212 --> 00:00:53.539
“All those baskets are food,” explained Akhom.

12
00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.336
“They only prepare that much food for the royal family.

13
00:00:57.337 --> 00:01:01.015
They must be going for a visit to the pyramid.”

14
00:01:01.016 --> 00:01:04.150
“Let’s jump on!” said Vinnie.

15
00:01:04.151 --> 00:01:09.800
The boys snuck into the small boat and hid among the food baskets.

16
00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:14.655
In the larger boat, twenty men picked up their long oars.

17
00:01:14.656 --> 00:01:18.007
They pushed and pulled the oars.

18
00:01:18.008 --> 00:01:24.147
The wind filled the gigantic sail and the small boat followed.

19
00:01:24.148 --> 00:01:27.279
The boys sailed down the Nile.

20
00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:35.341
From the boat, Vinnie could see all kinds of interesting things off shore.

21
00:01:35.342 --> 00:01:39.885
A farmer pushed a wooden plough through a field of wheat.

22
00:01:39.886 --> 00:01:43.670
Another large ship sailed beside them.

23
00:01:43.671 --> 00:01:47.142
It carried a huge white block of stone.

24
00:01:47.143 --> 00:01:50.879
“What’s that?” he whispered to Akhom.

25
00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.750
“That’s one of the blocks used for building a pyramid,” Akhom answered.

26
00:01:55.751 --> 00:01:59.535
“Pyramids are made of hundreds of heavy blocks of stone.”

27
00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:03.906
“That must take a lot of time and work,” said Vinnie.

28
00:02:03.907 --> 00:02:09.349
“Some say we make more stones than there are stars,” explained Akhom.

29
00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:12.355
“Thousands of people work on the Pharaoh’s pyramid.

30
00:02:12.356 --> 00:02:16.606
They started to build it before I was born.”

31
00:02:16.607 --> 00:02:18.733
“When will it be finished?”

32
00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:22.007
Vinnie asked in a surprised voice.

33
00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:26.206
Akhom shrugged. “Perhaps in a couple of years.

34
00:02:26.207 --> 00:02:30.154
Maybe by the time I marry.”

35
00:02:30.155 --> 00:02:35.625
Suddenly Vinnie saw a pair of blinking eyes staring from the water.

36
00:02:35.626 --> 00:02:40.487
“Akhom! Is that a crocodile?” Vinnie pointed.

37
00:02:40.488 --> 00:02:42.493
Akhom shook his head.

38
00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:44.379
“No, that’s a hippo.

39
00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.649
Look! There’s a crocodile!”

40
00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:52.045
Akhom pointed to a reptile lying in the sand.

41
00:02:52.046 --> 00:02:56.361
Further on the shore, they could see the Pharaoh’s pyramid.

42
00:02:56.362 --> 00:02:58.675
The boats slowed down.

43
00:02:58.676 --> 00:03:01.957
Men shouted orders at each other.

44
00:03:01.958 --> 00:03:06.923
“When we reach the shore, run for the pyramid,” Akhom instructed.

45
00:03:06.924 --> 00:03:14.756
When the boys jumped off the boat, Vinnie was surprised by the sight of the pyramid in real life.

46
00:03:14.757 --> 00:03:21.419
“Whoa!” he said, as he stopped to look up at the huge structure.

47
00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.391
Facing the sunset, the pyramid looked very majestic.

48
00:03:26.392 --> 00:03:31.373
Each side of its base was the length of two soccer fields.

49
00:03:31.374 --> 00:03:36.489
Though it seemed already quite tall, the workers were adding more blocks.

50
00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:42.172
Vinnie saw thousands of men pulling the heavy white blocks of stone.

51
00:03:42.173 --> 00:03:45.963
The boys climbed a ramp that led into the pyramid.

52
00:03:45.964 --> 00:03:48.646
Behind them, a voice shouted,

53
00:03:48.647 --> 00:03:52.206
“You, boys, stop! What are you doing here?”

54
00:03:52.207 --> 00:03:57.744
"The guards!” yelled Akhom. “Run, Vinnie! Run!”

55
00:03:57.745 --> 00:04:01.637
The boys ran up a ramp toward the pyramid.

56
00:04:01.638 --> 00:04:08.161
The guards followed closely behind.
